==Swedish==

===Etymology===
{{contraction|sv}} of earlier {{m|sv|eder}}, from {{inh|sv|gmq-osw|iþer}}, {{m|gmq-osw|idher}}, from {{inh|sv|non|iðʀ}}, from {{inh|sv|gem-pro|*izwiz}}, dative/accusative of {{m|gem-pro|*jūz}}, from {{der|sv|ine-pro|*yúHs}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|sv|/eːr/}}

===Pronoun===
{{head|sv|pronoun|g=c|neuter possessive only|ert|plural|era}}

# [[you]] ''(plural, object)''
#: {{syn|sv|eder|q1=formal, archaic}}
# {{lb|sv|possessive}} [[your]], [[yours]]; (speaking to more than one person, about one object)
#: {{syn|sv|eran|eder|q1=informal|q2=formal, archaic}}
# {{lb|sv|reflexive pronoun}} {{n-g|reflexive of '''[[ni]]'''; compare [[yourselves]]}}
#: {{ux|sv|Skulle ni vilja lära '''er''' jonglera?|Would you guys like to learn how to juggle?}}

====Usage notes====
* See ''[[ni]]'' for a note on its use as a courteous 2nd person singular.
* Even though ''er'' (2) and its archaic form ''[[eder]]'' is the possessive pronoun, it does have a genitive form ''[[ers]]'' and ''[[eders]]'', which is only used in expressions like {{m|sv|Ers Majestät||Your Majesty}} and {{m|sv|Ers Höghet||Your Highness}}.

