==Welsh==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|cy|/ɛr/}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|cy|wlm|yr}}, from {{inh|cy|cel-bry-pro|*er}}, from {{inh|cy|cel-pro|*ɸeri}}, ultimately from {{der|cy|ine-pro|*per-|t=in front}}. Compare {{cog|kw|er|t=for, by}}, {{cog|grc|περί|t=about, peri-}}, {{cog|la|per|t=through}}.<ref>{{R:cy:GPC}}</ref>

====Conjunction====
{{head|cy|conjunction}}

# [[although]]
#* {{quote-journal|cy|date=September 28, 2018|work=BBC Cymru Fyw| title=[https://www.bbc.co.uk/cymrufyw/45670189 Cymraeg y Wladfa a Chymraeg Cymru - beth yw'r gwahaniaethau?]| passage=Nid y Sbaeneg ('''er''' y byddai hynny'n syniad da hefyd) ond Cymraeg arbennig y Wladfa.|t=Not Spanish ('''although''' that would also be a good idea) but the particular Welsh of Y Wladfa.}}
#* {{quote-journal|cy|date=June 13, 2019|author=Llinos Lee|work=BBC Cymru Fyw| title=[https://www.bbc.co.uk/cymrufyw/48622604 Y Barri: Mwy na dim ond 'Gavin & Stacey']| passage=Ges i fy magu yn Y Barri, ac '''er''' mod i wedi symud i ffwrdd i'r brifysgol, …|t=I was brought up in Barry, and '''although''' I moved away for university, …}}

====Preposition====
{{head|cy|preposition|triggers soft mutation}}

# {{lb|cy|literary}} [[since]]
#: {{syn|cy|ers}}
# {{lb|cy|archaic}} [[in spite of]], [[despite]]
#: {{syn|cy|er gwaethaf}}
# {{lb|cy|archaic}} [[in order to]]
#: {{syn|cy|er mwyn|i}}
# {{lb|cy|archaic}} [[for the sake of]]
#: {{syn|cy|er mwyn}}
# {{lb|cy|obsolete}} [[because of]]
#: {{syn|cy|achos|o achos|oherwydd|oblegid}}
# {{lb|cy|obsolete}} [[for]], [[in exchange for]]
#: {{syn|cy|am}}
# {{lb|cy|obsolete}} [[resulting in]]
# {{lb|cy|obsolete}} [[through]]
#: {{syn|cy|trwy|drwy}}

====Usage notes====
* In very formal or literary language, {{m|cy|er}} is used when a specific start time is mentioned. 
:: {{ux|cy|Saif y castell yma '''er''' 1284.|The castle has stood here '''since''' 1284.}}
:: {{ux|cy|Y mae’r castell yn adfail '''er''' pan fu farw’r brenin olaf.|The castle has been a ruin '''since''' the last king died.}}
:{{m|cy|ers|Ers}} is used when the beginning of the time period is not mentioned.
:: {{ux|cy|Mae’r castell yma '''ers''' canrifoedd.|The castle has been here '''for''' centuries.}}
:In less formal registers, {{m|cy|ers}} is used in all instances.

====Derived terms====
* {{l|cy|er mwyn||for the sake of; in order to}}
* {{l|cy|er gwaethaf||despite}}
* {{l|cy|ers||since}}

